 "literal": "Ploughmen to the people of the world [are the] linchpin, bearing all those who rise unable to do that.",
 "translation": "Farmers are the linchpin of the world, for they support all those who take up other work because they cannot do that.",
 "modern": "உழவுத் தொழிலைச் செய்ய முடியாமல் வேறு தொழில்களைச் செய்யப் போகின்றவர் எல்லாரையும் தாங்குவதால், உழவர்களே உலகத்தவர்க்கு அச்சாணி ஆவார்கள்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet compares farmers to the linchpin of a chariot. Just as a linchpin holds the wheels and the entire weight of the chariot, farmers support the entire world. They bear the burden of feeding all those who take up other professions because they are unable to do the hard work of farming. The word 'ஆணி' (linchpin) perfectly captures their central, indispensable role in sustaining human society.",
